# NOTES: empty memo, appended lines, escaping both ways, replace by SET.
> ITEM NOTES 2
< +DATA
< .
> ITEM NOTES 2 ADD="first line"
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2 ADD="back\\slash \"quoted\" tab\x09end"
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2 ADD="two\nlines"
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2 ADD=""
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2 ADD=.dot
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2 ADD="del\x7Fbyte"
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2 ADD="trailing"
< +OK
# An L line does not escape TAB, so the expected line with "tab" below
# holds a literal tab.
> ITEM NOTES 2
< +DATA
< L first line
< L back\\slash "quoted" tab	end
< L two
< L lines
< L
< L .dot
< L del\x7Fbyte
< L trailing
< .
> ITEM NOTES 2 ADD="bad\x01byte"
< -ERR 102 bad memo text FIELD=NOTES
> ITEM NOTES 2 ADD="bad\x0Dcr"
< -ERR 102 bad memo text FIELD=NOTES
> ITEM SET 2 NOTES="replaced\nmemo"
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2
< +DATA
< L replaced
< L memo
< .
> ITEM SET 2 NOTES=""
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2
< +DATA
< .
> ITEM NOTES 9
< -ERR 200 no such item
> ITEM NOTES 9 ADD=x
< -ERR 200 no such item
> ITEM NOTES
< -ERR 102 missing argument FIELD=ID
> ITEM NOTES 2 3
< -ERR 100 too many arguments
> ITEM NOTES 2 TEXT=x
< -ERR 102 unexpected key FIELD=TEXT
> ITEM NOTES 1 ADD=x NEW=y
< -ERR 102 bad or missing argument FIELD=NEW
> ITEM NOTES 2 NEW=x END=y
< -ERR 102 bad or missing argument FIELD=END

# A memo saved in parts: NEW= starts the session's stage, PART= adds a
# line to it, and END= adds its line and makes the stage the memo; until
# then the memo is as it was.  The stage ends with its END=, and belongs
# to one record; a NEW= replaces it, and a PART= refused for its text
# leaves it as it was.
> ITEM SET 2 NOTES=old
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2 NEW="one\ntwo"
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2 PART=three
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2
< +DATA
< L old
< .
> ITEM NOTES 2 END=four
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2
< +DATA
< L one
< L two
< L three
< L four
< .
> ITEM NOTES 2 END=five
< -ERR 204 no note being saved FIELD=NOTES
> ITEM NOTES 2 NEW=a
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 1 PART=b
< -ERR 204 no note being saved FIELD=NOTES
> ITEM NOTES 2 NEW=c
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2 PART="bad\x0Dcr"
< -ERR 102 bad memo text FIELD=NOTES
> ITEM NOTES 9 PART=x
< -ERR 200 no such item
> ITEM NOTES 2 END=d
< +OK
> ITEM NOTES 2
< +DATA
< L c
< L d
< .

# A memo grows to ENG_MAXMEMO bytes and no further: nine lines of 200
# bytes and the CR LFs between them take 1816, a tenth line is refused,
# 182 more bytes fill the memo exactly, and then even an empty line is
# refused.  A line of exactly PROTO_MEMOLINE bytes is sent as one L line.
> ITEM NOTES 4 ADD="01234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789"
< +OK
